version: 2.0.0
description: |
  Memory Steward core (A1) — the pure scoring + clustering orchestrator over the
  native Claude Code memory store parsed by @a-company/premise-core's
  #native-memory-scan (A0). No I/O, no cross-package runtime dependency: consumes
  ParsedMemoryEntry, produces MemoryScore / MemoryFinding. Design settled in
  TD-2026-09-19-110. Hooks / CLI registration are a later pass.
components:
  memory-steward-types:
    description: Contract for the Steward — MemoryScore (scored ParsedMemoryEntry with age/type/graph breakdown + optional clusterId) and MemoryFinding (deduplicable prune/route/merge/pin suggestion with anti-nag expiresAt).
    type: model
    tags:
      - memory-steward
      - types
    path: types.ts
  memory-steward-score:
    description: scoreEntry composes a 0..1 staleness score from age (mtimeMs, normalized to a 90d horizon), per-type decay weight (project fast, feedback/reference/user slow), and graph-validity penalty. deriveFinding maps a score to a suggested action (provably-stale→prune, feedback→route:habits, project→route:task, reference+decision→route:decisions, near-dup→merge, durable→pin). Age/window constants re-defined locally to avoid a paradigm-mcp dependency.
    type: engine
    tags:
      - memory-steward
      - scoring
    path: score.ts
  memory-steward-cluster:
    description: clusterEntries detects near-duplicate memory bodies via normalized-token Jaccard (threshold ~0.6) + union-find; assigns deterministic clusterIds to clustered entries (singletons omitted). Pure, no LLM.
    type: engine
    tags:
      - memory-steward
      - clustering
    path: cluster.ts
  memory-steward-sync:
    description: >-
      B2 sync engine (advisory + strictly guarded, reworked 2026-09-20 after a dry-run against a real
      hand-curated MEMORY.md false-flagged active sections). computeSync (read-only) leans the native
      MEMORY.md and reports what WOULD change. DEMOTION is drastically narrowed: a block is demotable
      ONLY if it is a LEAF at heading level ≥3 (never a # title or ## section, never a node with child
      subsections) AND provably graph-stale (cites symbols, all dead vs the live graph) AND carries NO
      active-signal marker (⭐, START HERE, ACTIVE, IN PROGRESS, live, current, next, TODO, WIP, ⚠, or
      any date within 180d of now, case-insensitive) AND has no active-marked ancestor (protection
      inherits down the subtree). The old shipped+dated-old heuristic is REMOVED. PROJECTION is
      OFF by default (opts.project) — a plain sync only leans; when opted in the managed block
      (<!-- PARADIGM:BEGIN/END -->) is COMPACT (one terse `- [kind] title` line each, ≤80 chars),
      CAPPED at 8 items, and DEDUPED against the current file (skip any item whose id/title already
      appears — kills the circular re-injection case); 0 survivors → no block at all. Dedup of
      exact-duplicate leaf blocks (keep first) is unchanged. writeSyncResult is the ONLY mutator:
      backup-to-.bak FIRST, then atomic temp+rename, fail-open on any error (original untouched).
      Deterministic (no timestamps in the managed block) → two syncs over unchanged inputs are
      byte-identical. Includes a dependency-free unified-ish line diff for the advisory preview.
    type: engine
    tags:
      - memory-steward
      - sync
      - native-first
    path: sync.ts
